# what tools/metal-run.sh gives this phone (docs/porting/index.md): its big core and cores, its panel's rate,
# how many threads copy frames, how often the touch screen is read. A line of boot-arguments; # is a comment.
# fb_intf=<physical> as well, if its SoC's display interface is known: frames are then written behind the scan.
# panther (gs201): 8 cores = 2x X1 (cpu6-7) + 2x A78 (cpu4-5) + 4x A55 (cpu0-3); panel 1080x2400 @ 90 Hz.
# bootcpu=0 assumed (Exynos ABL enters the kernel on the first little core) — verify at M1 on hardware.
# fb_threads=4 for 90 Hz (redwood uses 6 at 120 Hz); touch_poll 4 ms as upstream.
bootcpu=0 cpus=8 fb_hz=90 fb_threads=4 touch_poll_us=4000
